Note for zoomers: this file describes critical changes to the source
code that could introduce bugs, cause Git conflicts on a merge or break
existing patches in general. If you are looking for a list of
user-facing changes, check the NEWS.md file.

2025-08-08  @danirod

        * cartero-objects/src/response.rs: Response has a new function
        called is_binary().
        * src/widgets/endpoint/response_panel.rs: the
        CarteroResponsePanel widget has a new action called
        response.force-binary-render.

2025-08-07  @danirod

        * cartero-objects/src/request_body.rs: A new value has been
        added to RequestBodyFile: 'RequestBodyFile::File'.

        * cartero-http/src/request.rs: BoundRequest now requires the
        RequestEnvironment in order to be instantiated. Therefore,
        BoundRequest::try_from() has been replaced by
        BoundRequest::new(), so that the function can accept two
        arguments.
        * cartero-http/src/request.rs: BoundRequest is now async.

        * cartero-http/src/body.rs: BoundBody::try_from() has been
        replaced by BoundBody::new(), because the function is async
        now.

2025-08-05  @danirod

        * ChangeLog: starting a ChangeLog. I've reviewed the Git
        repository to add the most important changes to this file
        made in the last couple of months.

2025-08-01  @danirod

        Cartero has switched to using the HTTP client provided by the
        cartero_http and cartero_isahc_client crates and has removed
        the cartero::client module.

        * src/client/*: the mod has been deleted.
        * src/widgets/endpoint/endpoint_pane.rs: sending an HTTP
        request will now pass the Request object to
        cartero_isahc_client::request().
        * src/updates/checker.rs: the updates checker will now use the
        new HTTP client when querying the GitHub API for app updates.

2025-08-01  @danirod

        Cartero has replaced some user interface widgets with new ones
        that are automatically binding their state to the properties of
        the objects from cartero_objects they map.

        For instance, the new pane for HTTP basic auth parameters is
        now automatically bound to the target
        RequestAuthenticationBasic object and has bidirectional
        bindings to make sure that it always reflect the state of the
        object, and that changes to the widgets are pushed back to the
        original object.

        * src/widgets/key_value_row.rs: module is removed because the
        widget has been replaced.
        * src/widgets/key_value_pane.rs: same.
        * data/ui/key_value_row.blp: UI file for the removed widget.
        * data/ui/key_value_pane.blp: same.
        * src/widgets/field: adds the new components for the FieldTable
        and related components.
        * data/ui/field_list_box_row.blp: new UI component for fields.
        * data/ui/field_placeholder_row: new UI component for the
        placeholder.
        * data/ui/field_list_box_row.blp: new UI component for the
        field table.

        * src/widgets/authorization_pane.rs: module is removed
        * src/widgets/authentication_pane/*: module is added to replace
        the old cartero::widgets::authorization_pane.
        * data/ui/authorization_pane.blp: is removed because it points
        to the old widget.
        * data/ui/authentication_pane.blp: replaces the old
        AuthorizationPane.
        * data/ui/basic_auth_pane.blp: UI pane for the new
        BasicAuthPane.
        * data/ui/bearer_auth_pane.blp: UI pane for the new
        BearerAuthPane.

        * src/widgets/request_body/*: module is removed
        * src/widgets/req_body/*: module is added to replace the old
        cartero::widgets::request_body module
        * data/ui/request_body_pane.blp: UI file is removed because it
        points to the old widget.
        * data/ui/urlencoded_body_pane.blp: UI file for the new
        UrlencodedBodyPane widget.
        * data/ui/multipart_body_pane.blp: UI file for the new
        MultipartBodyPane widget.
        * data/ui/raw_body_pane.blp: UI pane for the new RawBodyPane
        widget.
        * data/ui/request_body_pane.blp: UI pane for the new
        RequestBodyPane widget.

2025-08-01  @danirod

        Cartero has switched to using the cartero_file_format crate for
        all the file open and save needs, and converting a request into
        the .toml files used to store request data.

        * cartero_file_format: API stabilized.
        * src/file.rs: the module has been removed.
        * src/widgets/endpoint/endpoint_pane.rs: uses the new functions
        from cartero_file_format to serialize and deserialize a
        request.
        * src/win.rs: uses the new structs from cartero_interop to
        handle errors and show failure dialogs.

2025-08-01  @danirod

        Cartero has switched to using the data structures from the
        cartero_objects crate and has removed structures from the
        cartero::entities module.

        * src/entities/*: the mod has been removed
        * src/objects/*: the mod has been removed
        * src/widgets/endpoint_pane.rs: mod has moved to
        cartero::widgets::endpoint::endpoint_pane.
        * src/widgets/endpoint/endpoint_pane.rs: is now reactive and
        EndpointPane has a new property called 'request' to store the
        associated Request object. References to EndpointData have
        changed.
        * src/export/curl.rs: uses the new data structures to export as
        cURL.
        * src/updates/checker.rs: the updates checker will now use the
        new data structures to craft the HTTP request to the GitHub
        API.

2025-07-29  @danirod

        * cartero-objects/src/request_body_raw.rs: the 'payload'
        property from the RequestBodyRaw object has changed its type
        from glib::Bytes to String, so that

2025-07-23  @danirod

        * cartero-objects/src/field_table.rs: the FieldTable struct has
        a new method called 'reconcile()' to quickly update the Fields
        of a table

2025-07-11 @danirod

        The Export as cURL tab has moved to a toolbar button and it's
        now a stateless modal instead of a stateful panel that renders
        all the time.

        * src/widgets/export_tab/service.rs: moved to
        cartero::export::curl, src/export/curl.rs.

        * data/ui/export_tab.blp: UI pane for the removed widget.
        * data/ui/code_export_panel.blp: UI pane for the removed
        widget.
        * src/widgets/export_tab/tab.rs: removed because there is no
        tab anymore.
        * src/widgets/export_tab/base.rs: same.
        * src/widgets/export_tab/code.rs: same.

        * data/ui/export_dialog.blp: UI pane for the new export dialog
        used to export a payload.
        * src/widgets/export_dialog.rs: Rust code for the new dialog.
        * src/widgets/endpoint_pane.rs: has a new function called
        'export_request()' to trigger the export dialog in the desired
        format.
        * src/file_dialogs.rs: has a new function called
        'export_file()' to trigger a save dialog that takes any file
        extension.

        * data/ui/main_window.blp: has a new button to trigger the
        export dropdown.
        * data/ui/main_window_no_csd.blp: same for the non-CSD version.
